scription":"DISPLAY-ONLY: renders fonts as inline visual specimen cards; it does NOT recommend or find fonts. You MUST first call font_recommend, font_search, or font_similar to get real fonts, then pass a real font identifier here. If both font_id and postscript_name are supplied, font_id takes precedence — NEVER invent font identifiers or call this without fetching real ones first. Pass every font you want to preview together in one call as a font_identifiers list (up to 10 entries) — do not call this tool once per font. WHEN TO USE: after font_recommend, font_search, or font_similar, to show what each font looks like; or when the user says 'show this font', 'preview this font', 'what does this font look like'. The returned card reflects the font that resolved and includes resolvedVia when applicable. On success, cards render automatically — reply with nothing, and never narrate this tool, its arguments, or how the call must be shaped in chat. On failure, briefly tell the user the preview could not be generated and why (e.g. font not found), without narrating tool internals.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"font_identifiers":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/FontIdentifier"},"title":"Font Identifiers","type":"array"},"locale":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":"en_US","title":"Locale"}},"required":["font_identifiers"],"$defs":{"FontIdentifier":{"description":"A font's identity: mandatory postscript_name, optional font_id. Shared\nacross tools that consume this differently -- font_id is tried first in\nget_font_details/get_font_styles/get_font_preview, used to skip a\nresolution hop in add_fonts_to_cc_selections, and accepted but never\nconsumed in create_font_kit or get_similar_fonts (both look up by\npostscript_name alone) -- see each tool's own docstring for which\napplies.","properties":{"postscript_name":{"title":"Postscript Name","type":"string"},"font_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Font Id"}},"required":["postscript_name"],"title":"FontIdentifier","type":"object"}},"title":"get_font_previewArguments"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"ui/resourceUri":"ui://af-fonts-preview/card.html","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://af-fonts-preview/card.html"},"resource_name":"adobe.font_preview","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/font_preview","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}}},{"name":"adobe.interactive_image_blur_background_app","title":"Blur background","description":"**Session handle:** each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) has its own `sessionId`, minted on demand — it is not one handle for the whole conversation. The **first** call for a given source image must pass `sessionId: -1`; wait for the `sessionId` it returns and reuse that value for every later call on that same image. When `originalUploadedImage` changes to a different image, pass `-1` again to start that image's session, and keep a per-image mapping so returning to an earlier image reuses its `sessionId`.\n\nBlur background of the image to make the main subject stand out. This tool uses the Gaussian Blur effect to blur the background. For other types of blur effects, use the interactive_image_apply_effects_app tool instead.\n\n**ROUTING — this widget owns every single-image request for background blur behind a subject.** Count only the images this turn asks you to edit, not what the session holds.\n- **1 image this turn:** call THIS tool. Never ask widget-vs-server-side; never offer the direct tools (`image_apply_lens_blur`, `image_apply_gaussian_blur`, or `image_apply_effects`).\n- **2+ images this turn:** NEVER this tool — no batch form; use those direct tools and do not mention this one.\n- **1-image exceptions, use those direct tools when:** the user explicitly asks you to do it for them (\"just do it\", \"you pick\") — an explicit ask only, never inferred from terseness, a stated value, or impatience; no subject mask is available or obtainable (this tool requires one).\n- **STOP after calling.** It renders its own result and returns no asset URL — no `asset_inline_preview`, `asset_preview_file`, `interactive_image_edit_preview`, or any next step.\n- **Non-generative** — never widens what generative editing is permitted.\n\n**Requires a mask:**\n- If no maskURI exists for this image, call image_select_subject_action_json tool first.\n- Verify the mask was generated from the same image being edited.\n- The mask required for this tool must be the background mask.\n   → If the mask is the subject mask, set toBeInverted to true.\n   → If the mask is the background mask, set toBeInverted to false.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"imageURI":{"type":"string","description":"The image to edit (accessible http/https URL). Choose by first match: (1) a new image uploaded with this request; (2) the previous tool's `outputUrl` if it just produced one; (3) the SAME `imageURI` you passed to the previous `*_app` edit — reuse it so consecutive effects stack on one base (a 2nd effect uses the 1st's input, NOT its result); (4) `originalUploadedImage`, the session's source image. NEVER use `currentInputImage` or any rendition — that is the flattened result and is for destructive tools only. Don't call `image_get_context` for this."},"originalUploadedImage":{"type":"string","description":"The source image this edit session is built on, and the key its `sessionId` is bound to. If an image was just uploaded to chat, use its reference; otherwise copy `originalUploadedImage` verbatim from the widget state of the image you are editing. It MUST stay constant while you keep editing the same image — NEVER set it to an edited, rendition, or tool-output image, which starts a new, empty history and loses prior edits. Each distinct `originalUploadedImage` has its own `sessionId`: whenever this changes to a different source image, pass `sessionId: -1` to start a new session for it."},"sessionId":{"type":"string","description":"The widget-state session handle, unique to each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) — not one handle for the whole conversation. Set it to the `sessionId` a previous image tool returned for the image you are editing now. If that image has no `sessionId` yet (a newly uploaded image, or you switched to a different one), set it to `-1`; a new handle is minted and returned — reuse that value for every later call on this image. Keep a `sessionId` per source image: returning to an earlier image reuses the handle from that image, not `-1`."},"mask":{"type":"object","properties":{"maskURI":{"type":"string","description":"The URI of the mask to be applied to the image. **Reusing a mask (only when the editing context with `actionHistory` is available):** the user can edit or remove masks in the editor, so a mask URL you passed earlier may be stale — the context's `actionHistory` lists each edit with its current mask. To carry a mask forward from an earlier edit, find that edit's most recent entry and pass its `mask.maskURI`, not the URL you originally passed; `isMaskUpdated` means the user edited it, so keep `maskDescription` / `toBeInverted` unchanged. If the entry has `userRemovedMaskURI` instead of `maskURI`, the user removed that mask: don't reuse it — call a selection tool if the request still targets that region, and pass `userRemovedMaskURI` only if the user explicitly asks for that mask again. To use the original AI selection instead of the user's edit, or after a crop, expand, straighten or undo-all, call a selection tool again. Use the attached context when present; call `interactive_image_get_context` only when none is attached."},"maskDescription":{"type":"string","description":"The description of what the mask is selecting."},"toBeInverted":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the mask should be inverted, in order to select the inverted area."}},"required":["maskURI","maskDescription","toBeInverted"]},"replaceLastEdit":{"description":"Boolean value that tells the widget to undo the previous effect before applying the next requested.\n**For Example** a prompt like \"undo the last effect and apply a twirl\" would set this boolean to true to undo the last effect before applying what is requested in this prompt. With this input parameter the undoEdit tool does not need to be called before calling the next effect tool","type":"boolean"}},"required":["imageURI","originalUploadedImage","sessionId","mask"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://widget/pure-editor-carousel.html","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Blurring background","openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Blurred background","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://widget/pure-editor-carousel.html"},"resource_name":"adobe.interactive_image_blur_background_app","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/interactive_image_blur_background_app","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"description":"If failed, error message from the tool result.","type":"string"},"input":{"description":"Original input parameters passed to the tool","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"metadata":{"description":"Optional metadata