context has a URN (urn:aaid:...) and no presigned URL is available.\n\nWHEN NOT TO USE:\n- If context already has a presigned URL (https://cc-api-storage.adobe.io/... or similar), use that URL directly.\n","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"asset_ids":{"minItems":1,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"One or more unique identifiers of the source assets"}},"required":["asset_ids"]},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"ui":{"visibility":["app"]},"resource_name":"adobe.asset_get_presigned_url","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/asset_get_presigned_url","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","type":"object","properties":{"assets":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"assetId":{"description":"Adobe Creative Cloud asset URN","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"Display name of the asset","type":"string"},"mediaType":{"description":"MIME type of the asset (e.g. image/jpeg)","type":"string"},"source":{"description":"Asset source: acp (Creative Cloud), lightroom, or stock","type":"string","enum":["acp","lightroom","stock"]},"presignedAssetUrl":{"description":"Time-limited presigned URL for the primary asset.","type":"string","format":"uri"},"presignedRenditionUrl":{"description":"Time-limited presigned URL for a rendition of the asset. For native image types (image/jpg, image/jpeg, image/png) this is the same URL as presignedAssetUrl (full-resolution original). For other asset types it is a full-size rendition from the Rendition Service when available, and will be absent if renditions are unsupported for the asset type.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uri"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":{}}}},"required":["assets"],"additionalProperties":{}}},{"name":"adobe.image_apply_effects","title":"Apply Effects","description":"**Reusing a mask (only when the editing context with `actionHistory` is available):** the user can edit or remove masks in the editor, so a mask URL you passed earlier may be stale — the context's `actionHistory` lists each edit with its current mask. To carry a mask forward from an earlier edit, find that edit's most recent entry and pass its `mask.maskURI`, not the URL you originally passed; `isMaskUpdated` means the user edited it, so keep `maskDescription` / `toBeInverted` unchanged. If the entry has `userRemovedMaskURI` instead of `maskURI`, the user removed that mask: don't reuse it — call a selection tool if the request still targets that region, and pass `userRemovedMaskURI` only if the user explicitly asks for that mask again. To use the original AI selection instead of the user's edit, or after a crop, expand, straighten or undo-all, call a selection tool again. Use the attached context when present; call `interactive_image_get_context` only when none is attached.\n\n**ROUTING — `interactive_image_apply_effects_app` owns single-image artistic effects and filters.** Count only the images this turn asks you to edit, not what the session holds.\n- **1 image this turn:** call `interactive_image_apply_effects_app`, not this tool. Never ask the user to choose; never offer a server-side edit.\n- **2+ images this turn:** THIS tool for the whole set — `interactive_image_apply_effects_app` has no batch form; never call or mention it.\n- **1-image exceptions, use THIS tool when:** the user explicitly asks you to do it for them (\"just do it\", \"you pick\") — an explicit ask only, never inferred from terseness, a stated value, or impatience; `options.effect` is `colorOverlay` — not in the widget; `interactive_image_apply_effects_app` is unavailable; the output feeds another tool, not the user.\n\nApplies a single Photoshop filter/style effect to the image or an area, chosen via `options.effect`.\n\n**Effects — set `options.effect` to one of:**\n- `grain`: film grain, analog grain, add grain, cinematic texture, grainy photo, shot on film.\n- `noise`: add noise, digital noise, pixel noise, noisy image, uniform noise, digital texture.\n- `colorOverlay`: color overlay, color wash, tint filter, color layer on photo. Adds a new flat-color layer on top — a graphic/stylized tint. For a natural-looking global warm/cool or color-cast shift that preserves existing lighting, shadows, and detail, use `image_apply_adjustments`'s color temperature or HSL params instead. **Cannot set opacity** — for \"at 20%\"/semi-transparent requests use `image_fill_area`. Without a mask covers the whole canvas. **Do not use** to fill or replace a background behind a subject (even a transparent cutout); use `image_remove_background` with `options.backgroundColor` instead.\n- `gaussianBlur`: blur, soften, defocus, bokeh, out of focus, hazy background. Uniform-radius; for falloff/shallow depth-of-field use `image_apply_lens_blur`. To blur the background behind a subject, the `interactive_image_blur_background_app` routing rule above applies.\n- `glitch`: glitch, chromatic aberration, broken screen, VHS distortion, cyberpunk. Larger absolute offset = more intense.\n- `halftone`: halftone, dot pattern, comic book, newspaper, screen printing, risograph.\n- `monochromaticTint`: black and white, grayscale, sepia, duotone, faded, washed out, single color wash.\n\n**One effect per call** — to layer several, call once per effect, chaining each result's `outputUrl` into the next call's `imageURIs`.\n\nTo target a specific object or area in the image:\n1. If the user provides a mask URL, use it to limit the effect to that region.\n2. If no mask URL is provided but the user wants to target a specific area, first use available masking tools to create a mask based on their description, then apply the effect.\n3. If no mask is specified and no targeting is requested, apply the effect to the entire image.\n\n**Long-running batches:** A batch may take longer than a single call can wait. If the response is a single result with `status: \"working\"`, NO images are ready yet — call `image_get_task_status` with its `taskId` to collect them all at once. Do NOT call `image_apply_effects` again, which would redo the work and bill for it twice.\n\nExamples:\n- Noise via preset: { \"effect\": \"noise\", \"preset\": \"stronglyAddMoreNoise\" }\n- Red overlay, lighten blend: { \"effect\": \"colorOverlay\", \"color\": { \"red\": 205, \"green\": 3, \"blue\": 3 }, \"blendMode\": \"lighten\" }\n- Blur the background: { \"effect\": \"gaussianBlur\", \"blurRadius\": 5, \"blurTarget\": \"background\" }\n- Subtle glitch (negative offset): { \"effect\": \"glitch\", \"horizontalOffset\": -10 }\n- Sepia tint: { \"effect\": \"monochromaticTint\", \"hue\": 50, \"saturation\": 25, \"lightness\": 0 }","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"imageURIs":{"maxItems":10,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Identifies a list of images to process. For each image, when continuing from a previous tool call, use `outputUrl` or `presignedAssetUrl` from that tool's structured result for that entry when available. Otherwise, prefer full-resolution, fetchable URIs."},"outputFileType":{"default":"png","description":"Output format for the edited image. Use `\"png\"` for all image editing operations — PNG preserves lossless quality and transparency through multi-step workflows. Only use `\"jpeg\"` when the user has explicitly requested JPEG format.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","const":"png"},{"type":"string","const":"jpeg"}]},"maskURI":{"type":"string","description":"URI of a mask image where white pixels mark the region to edit and black pixels mark the region to preserve. When continuing from a previous tool call, use `outputUrl` or `presignedAssetUrl` from a mask-producing tool (e.g. `image_select_by_prompt`, `image_select_subject`, `image_invert_selection`) as `maskURI`. If none is available, call a selection tool first."},"options":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"grain"},"grainAmount":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":100,"description":"Amount of grain to add. Valid range: [0, 100]. Recommended: 40 moderate, 80 strong."}},"required":["effect","grainAmount"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"noise"},"noiseAmount":{"type":"number","minimum":0.1,"maximum":400,"description":"Noise amount as a percentage (Photoshop Add Noise). Valid range: [0.1, 400]. Recommended: 25 moderate, 50 strong."},"preset":{"description":"Named intensity preset. Provide this, `noiseAmount`, or both; preset alone picks a default, `noiseAmount` overrides when both are set.","type":"string","enum":["addMoreNoise","stronglyAddMoreNoise"]}},"required":["effect"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"colorOverlay"},"color":{"type":"object","properties":{"red":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":255},"green":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":255},"blue":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":255}},"required":["red","green","blue"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The RGB color for the fill layer. All three channels (red, green, blue) are required — even when a channel value is 0, it must be explicitly included."},"blendMode":{"type":"string","enum":["normal","dissolve","darken","multiply","colorBurn","linearBurn","darkerColor","lighten","screen","colorDodge","linearDodge","lighterColor","overlay","softLight","hardLight","vividLight","linearLight","pinLight","hardMix","difference","exclusion","blendSubtraction","blendDivide","hue","saturation","color","luminosity","passThrough"]},"layerName":{"type":"string"}},"required":["effect","color","blendMode"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"gaussianBlur"},"blurRadius":{"type":"number","minimum":0.1,"maximum":250,"description":"The radius of the blur in pixels. Valid range: [0.1,250]."},"blurTarget":{"type":"string","enum":["currentLayer","subject","background"]}},"required":["effect","blurRadius","blurTarget"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"glitch"},"horizontalOffset":{"default":-19,"description":"How far (in pixels) to shift the red channel. Negative values shift left, positive shift right. Range: -50 to 50. Default: -19.","type":"number","minimum":-50,"maximum":50}},"required":["effect"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"halftone"},"radius":{"type":"number","minimum":4,"maximum":127,"description":"Max halftone dot radius in pixels (Color Halftone). Valid range: [4, 127]. Typical values: 10, 15, 30."},"blackAndWhite":{"default":false,"type":"boolean","description":"If true, adds a black-to-white gradient map adjustment layer so the halftone reads as monochrome."},"layerID":{"type":"number","description":"The ID to assign to the duplicated layer. Default: 17 for color, 18 for B&W."},"layerName":{"type":"string"}},"required":["effect","radius"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"effect":{"type":"string","const":"monochromaticTint"},"hue":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":360,"description":"The hue value (0-360) for the tint."},"saturation":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":100,"description":"The saturation value for the tint (0-100). Recommended: 25."},"lightness":{"type":"number","minimum":-100,"maximum":100,"description":"The lightness value for the tint (-100 to 100). Recommended: 0."}},"required":["effect","hue","saturation","lightness"],"additionalProperties":false}]}},"required":["imageURIs","options"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"resource_name":"adobe.image_apply_effects","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/image_apply_effects","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"description":"If failed, error message from the tool result.","type":"string"},"input":{"description":"Original input parameters passed to the tool","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"metadata":{"description":"Optional metadata related to the tool result(s), will vary depending on the tool.","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"originalURI":{"description":"Original input image URI, if applicable.","type":"string"},"outputFile":{"description":"If tool succeeded, the file object for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputUrl":{"description":"If tool succeeded, presigned URL for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputMediaType":{"description":"If tool succeeded, IANA media type of the asset at `outputUrl` (e.g. \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"). Set when the tool knows the output format deterministically; clients should prefer this over inferring from the URL or following redirects.","type":"string"},"requestId":{"description":"Request ID for tracking and debugging.","type":"string"},"originRequestId":{"description":"Diagnostic id of the call that started a long-running operation; every poll of that operation reports the same value. Quote it when reporting a problem. NOT a `taskId` — never pass it to a tool.","type":"string"},"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the tool call was successful or not."},"importantNote":{"description":"Optional high-priority note for the assistant about this result: follow-up actions, caveats, or how to present or reuse the output.","type":"string"},"status":{"description":"Set to \"working\" when the operation is still running upstream and no output exists yet. The call did not fail — call the `image_get_task_status` tool with the returned `taskId` to wait for the result. Never present a \"working\" result to the user as a finished deliverable.","type":"string","const":"working"},"taskId":{"type":"string","description":"Opaque handle for an operation that is still running. Present when `status` is \"working\". Pass it verbatim to the `image_get_task_status` tool to wait for the result. Server-generated and meaningless to you — not an id you can look up, construct, or correlate with anything. Treat it as a blob."},"statusMessage":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable description of what the operation is currently doing. Safe to show the user as progress, but it is not a result — never treat it as one."},"pollInterval":{"type":"number","description":"Milliseconds to wait before calling `image_get_task_status` with this `taskId`. Normally 0: `image_get_task_status` blocks while it waits, so there is no reason to sleep first."}},"required":["success"],"additionalProperties":{}}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"adobe.image_apply_lens_blur","title":"Apply Lens Blur","description":"**ROUTING — `interactive_image_blur_background_app` owns single-image background blur behind a subject.** Count only the images this turn asks you to edit, not what the session holds.\n- **1 image this turn:** call `interactive_image_blur_background_app`, not this tool. Never ask the user to choose; never offer a server-side edit.\n- **2+ images this turn:** THIS tool for the whole set — `interactive_image_blur_background_app` has no batch form; never call or mention it.\n- **1-image exceptions, use THIS tool when:** the user explicitly asks you to do it for them (\"just do it\", \"you pick\") — an explicit ask only, never inferred from terseness, a stated value, or impatience; no subject mask is available or obtainable (the widget requires one); `interactive_image_blur_background_app` is unavailable; the output feeds another tool, not the user.\n\nBlurs the background with depth-of-field falloff (bokeh) while keeping the subject sharp. Auto-detects the primary subject and progressively blurs the background — no manual masking.\n\n**Output Format:** ALWAYS use `outputFileType: \"png\"`. PNG is required — it preserves lossless quality and transparency through multi-step edits and selection-mask chains. Only use `\"jpeg\"` when the user has explicitly requested JPEG format for the final result.\n\n**Use ONLY when the user explicitly asks for blur, bokeh, depth-of-field, or out-of-focus background.\n\nTakes no mask and ignores selection state — do not chain `image_select_subject` / `image_invert_selection` ahead of it; subject masking is built in.\n\nFor a uniform-radius blur instead of DoF falloff/bokeh, use `image_apply_gaussian_blur`: either `blurTarget: 'background'` (auto subject detection), or pass a `maskURI` from `image_select_subject` or `image_select_by_prompt` + `image_invert_selection` when you need a custom region or a sharper mask boundary.\n\nExample: <example> Apply lens blur: {} </example>","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"imageURI":{"type":"string","description":"A valid accessible image URL (http or https) of the image to edit. See the tool description for how to choose it."},"outputFileType":{"default":"png","description":"Output format for the edited image. Use `\"png\"` for all image editing operations — PNG preserves lossless quality and transparency through multi-step workflows. Only use `\"jpeg\"` when the user has explicitly requested JPEG format.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","const":"png"},{"type":"string","const":"jpeg"}]},"sessionId":{"description":"The widget-state session handle, unique to each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) — not one handle for the whole conversation. Set it to the `sessionId` a previous image tool returned for the image you are editing now. If that image has no `sessionId` yet (a newly uploaded image, or you switched to a different one), set it to `-1`; a new handle is minted and returned — reuse that value for every later call on this image. Keep a `sessionId` per source image: returning to an earlier image reuses the handle from that image, not `-1`.","type":"string"}},"required":["imageURI"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"resource_name":"adobe.image_apply_lens_blur","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/image_apply_lens_blur","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"description":"If failed, error message from the tool result.","type":"string"},"input":{"description":"Original input parameters passed to the tool","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"metadata":{"description":"Optional metadata related to the tool result(s), will vary depending on the tool.","type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{}},"originalURI":{"description":"Original input image URI, if applicable.","type":"string"},"outputFile":{"description":"If tool succeeded, the file object for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputUrl":{"description":"If tool succeeded, presigned URL for the processed image result.","type":"string"},"outputMediaType":{"description":"If tool succeeded, IANA media type of the asset at `outputUrl` (e.g. \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"). Set when the tool knows the output format deterministically; clients should prefer this over inferring from the URL or following redirects.","type":"string"},"requestId":{"description":"Request ID for tracking and debugging.","type":"string"},"originRequestId":{"description":"Diagnostic id of the call that started a long-running operation; every poll of that operation reports the same value. Quote it when reporting a problem. NOT a `taskId` — never pass it to a tool.","type":"string"},"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the tool call was successful or not."},"importantNote":{"description":"Optional high-priority note for the assistant about this result: follow-up actions, caveats, or how to present or reuse the output.","type":"string"}},"required":["success"],"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A single item in the tool response (a tool may return several). Check `success` first: when true, use `outputUrl` or `outputFile` when present for the main deliverable; when false, use `error` for the error message. Always read `importantNote` if set, regardless of whether the call succeeded or failed."}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Output from MCP tool call"}},{"name":"adobe.interactive_image_undo_edits_app","title":"Undo edits","description":"**Session handle:** each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) has its own `sessionId`, minted on demand — it is not one handle for the whole conversation. The **first** call for a given source image must pass `sessionId: -1`; wait for the `sessionId` it returns and reuse that value for every later call on that same image. When `originalUploadedImage` changes to a different image, pass `-1` again to start that image's session, and keep a per-image mapping so returning to an earlier image reuses its `sessionId`.\n\nUndo previous edits applied to an image by an Photoshop tool. When undoing multiple edits, make a single call with { numberOfEdits: N } to undo the last N edits. Do NOT make multiple sequential calls with { numberOfEdits: 1 }.\n\n**HOW TO USE THIS TOOL:**\n1. **Undo last N edits** (use numberOfEdits): When the user wants to step back through recent edits.\n   - User says \"undo\" or \"undo last\" → use { numberOfEdits: 1 } (undo only the last edit).\n   - User says \"undo last X\" or \"undo X edits\" → use { numberOfEdits: X }.\n2. **Undo by edit name** (use numberOfEdits): When the user wants to undo a specific edit by name, undo that edit and all subsequent edits after.\n   - **MUST** read the latest context and take the latest \"actionHistory\", see updateTimestamp. Find the matching edit in this list and derive the correct numberOfEdits from the **reverse chronological order** of applied edits. \n   - If the target edit is the first (oldest) entry in actionHistory, use revertToOriginal instead (step 3).\n   - i.e. edits applied in order: (1) apply hueSat, (2) remove background, (3) blur background. User says \"undo remove background\". The edit to undo is the 2nd from the end → use { numberOfEdits: 2 }.\n3. **Revert to original** (use revertToOriginal): Only when the user explicitly asks to remove ALL edits and return to the original image.\n   - User says \"undo all\", \"clear all\", \"start over\", etc → use { revertToOriginal: true }.\n   - Do NOT use revertToOriginal when the user only says \"undo\".\n\n**Implementation notes:**\n- This tool does NOT use generative AI, it manipulates the edit history directly (removes or reverts edits).\n- For `imageURI`, reuse the SAME image you passed to the previous `*_app` edit (or the previous tool's `outputUrl`, or the uploaded image) — never `currentInputImage` or a rendition.\n- If there are no edits to undo, inform the user instead of calling the tool.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"imageURI":{"type":"string","description":"The image to edit (accessible http/https URL). Choose by first match: (1) a new image uploaded with this request; (2) the previous tool's `outputUrl` if it just produced one; (3) the SAME `imageURI` you passed to the previous `*_app` edit — reuse it so consecutive effects stack on one base (a 2nd effect uses the 1st's input, NOT its result); (4) `originalUploadedImage`, the session's source image. NEVER use `currentInputImage` or any rendition — that is the flattened result and is for destructive tools only. Don't call `image_get_context` for this."},"originalUploadedImage":{"type":"string","description":"The source image this edit session is built on, and the key its `sessionId` is bound to. If an image was just uploaded to chat, use its reference; otherwise copy `originalUploadedImage` verbatim from the widget state of the image you are editing. It MUST stay constant while you keep editing the same image — NEVER set it to an edited, rendition, or tool-output image, which starts a new, empty history and loses prior edits. Each distinct `originalUploadedImage` has its own `sessionId`: whenever this changes to a different source image, pass `sessionId: -1` to start a new session for it."},"sessionId":{"type":"string","description":"The widget-state session handle, unique to each source image (`originalUploadedImage`) — not one handle for the whole conversation. Set it to the `sessionId` a previous image tool returned for the image you are editing now. If that image has no `sessionId` yet (a newly uploaded image, or you switched to a different one), set it to `-1`; a new handle is minted and returned — reuse that value for every later call on this image. Keep a `sessionId` per source image: returning to an earlier image reuses the handle from that image, not `-1`."},"undo":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"numberOfEdits":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Number of edits to undo, in reverse chronological order. Use 1 to undo only the last edit (e.g. when user says \"undo\"). Use 3 to undo the last 3 edits, etc."}},"required":["numberOfEdits"],"description":"Use when the user wants to undo one or more recent edits. Use numberOfEdits: 1 when the user says \"undo\" or \"undo last\" (undo last edit only). Use a larger number when they specify a count (e.g. \"undo last 3 edits\")."},{"type":"object","properties":{"revertToOriginal":{"type":"boolean","const":true}},"required":["revertToOriginal"],"description":"Use ONLY when the user explicitly asks to undo ALL edits and revert to the original image (e.g. \"undo all\", \"clear all edits\", \"start over\", \"reset to original\"). Do NOT use for a single \"undo\" — that is numberOfEdits: 1."}],"description":"Exactly one option: (1) numberOfEdits for undoing the last N edits, or (2) revertToOriginal: true for reverting to the original image. Default to numberOfEdits: 1 when the user says \"undo\" without \"all\" or a number."}},"required":["imageURI","originalUploadedImage","sessionId","undo"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":false,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false},"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://widget/pure-editor-carousel.html","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Undoing edits","openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Edits undone","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://widget/pure-editor-carousel.html"},"resource_name":"adobe.interactive_image_undo_edits_app","_codex_apps":{"resource_uri":"/connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c/link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e/interactive_image_undo_edits_app","contains_mcp_source":true},"connector_id":"connector_69312da8e4dc81919370cb86fd172b6c","connector_name":"Adobe","connector_description":"Design, combine, and edit","link_id":"link_6abb1a24e0d88191bee88b0fb41f697e","link_owner_profile":{}},"outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","prope